# 1. Purpose

The Automation Engine enables Aura to perform useful actions automatically when defined triggers and conditions are satisfied.

Automations must feel dependable, understandable and calm.

The user should be able to create workflows such as:

- Start Good Night at 23:00.
- Turn on hallway lights when motion is detected after sunset.
- Start Gaming when the television changes to the PlayStation input.
- Notify the user when an important device becomes unavailable.
- Run Movie Night when the user arrives home during the evening.

The Automation Engine coordinates trigger observation, condition evaluation, execution scheduling, Scene Engine handoff, loop prevention, persistence, diagnostics and user-facing history.

It must never behave like an unpredictable black box.

---

# 2. Product Goals

The Automation Engine shall:

- Allow users to create automations without technical terminology.
- Support time, solar, device, sensor, presence and scene-related triggers.
- Evaluate multiple conditions consistently.
- Execute Aura scenes and normalized device actions.
- Remain local-first whenever technically possible.
- Explain why an automation did or did not run.
- Prevent duplicate, recursive or rapidly repeated executions.
- Handle unavailable devices and partial failures gracefully.
- Preserve automation definitions while integrations are offline.
- Provide clear execution history and diagnostics.
- Respect iOS, HomeKit and background-execution limitations.
- Avoid excessive network, battery and background activity.
- Support future expansion without changing the core data model.

---

# 3. Non-Goals

Version 1 does not aim to:

- Replace Apple Home automations.
- Replace advanced home-automation servers such as Home Assistant.
- Provide unrestricted scripting or arbitrary code execution.
- Guarantee continuous background execution outside platform allowances.
- Run cloud-dependent automations without an explicitly designed cloud service.
- Expose raw vendor events to users.
- Provide complex variables, loops or programming constructs in the first release.
- Silently modify automations created in other ecosystems.
- Infer safety-critical actions without explicit user configuration.

Aura automations are intended for reliable everyday experiences, not unrestricted programming.

