# 6. System Responsibilities

The Automation Engine owns:

- Automation definition persistence.
- Trigger registration.
- Event normalization.
- Event deduplication.
- Debounce and cooldown behavior.
- Condition evaluation.
- Execution eligibility.
- Run scheduling.
- Scene Engine handoff.
- Direct normalized action execution.
- Correlation IDs and recursion prevention.
- Execution history.
- Automation health state.
- Diagnostics and user-facing explanations.

The Automation Engine does not own:

- Vendor-specific networking.
- Device discovery.
- Pairing credentials.
- Device capability detection.
- Scene action internals.
- HomeKit database ownership.
- Operating-system background scheduling guarantees.

