# 33. Concurrency Policies

```swift
enum AutomationConcurrencyPolicy: String, Codable, Sendable {
    case skipIfRunning
    case restart
    case queueOne
}
```

Default:

- `skipIfRunning`

Behavior:

## Skip If Running

A second trigger is recorded as skipped while the current run continues.

## Restart

The current run is cancelled safely and a new run begins.

Use only for actions known to be cancellation-safe.

## Queue One

One pending run may wait behind the current run.

Additional triggers are coalesced.

Unlimited queues are not permitted.

---

# 34. Cooldown Behavior

Cooldown begins when a run starts unless a future advanced option specifies completion-based cooldown.

A trigger received during cooldown should produce a lightweight skipped record.

Suggested user copy:

`Skipped because this automation ran recently.`

---

# 35. Loop and Recursion Prevention

Automation loops are a critical failure mode.

Example:

```text
Automation A turns TV on
TV-on event triggers Automation B
Automation B runs Scene X
Scene X turns TV off
TV-off event triggers Automation A
```

Aura shall use:

- Correlation IDs.
- Causation IDs.
- Execution ancestry.
- Maximum chain depth.
- Rapid-cycle detection.
- Per-automation cooldown.

Recommended maximum automation chain depth:

- 8

If the limit is reached, the next run must be blocked and diagnostics must explain the cycle.

