# 69. Acceptance Criteria

The Automation Engine is ready for initial release when:

1. Users can create an automation through a guided flow.
2. Time triggers support selected weekdays and time-zone changes.
3. Sunrise and sunset triggers support offsets when a valid home location exists.
4. Device-state and sensor events are normalized before evaluation.
5. Conditions support both `all` and `any` modes.
6. Conditions use a consistent state snapshot.
7. Stale security-relevant state never counts as confirmed.
8. Automations can run Aura scenes.
9. Automations can execute supported normalized device commands.
10. Wait and one-level conditional actions work within documented limits.
11. Duplicate events do not cause duplicate execution.
12. Cooldown and concurrency policies work predictably.
13. Direct and indirect automation loops are blocked.
14. Every run receives a correlation ID.
15. Skipped, successful, partial and failed runs are distinguished.
16. Execution history explains triggers, conditions and actions.
17. Invalid automations are preserved and marked `Needs Attention`.
18. Device removal or capability changes trigger revalidation.
19. Notification actions handle denied permission honestly.
20. The engine does not promise unsupported iOS background reliability.
21. Automation definitions and history remain local by default.
22. No vendor API object is exposed to the Automation Engine or SwiftUI layer.
23. Core scheduling, evaluation and loop protection are covered by automated tests.
24. Real-hardware scenarios pass for the initial supported setup.

